                    briefing_text_r3:       `Quinn's eight managerial roles span the four quadrants — Mentor/Facilitator (Clan), Innovator/Broker (Adhocracy), Producer/Director (Market), Monitor/Coordinator (Hierarchy). A leader who only plays Producer/Director loses the people; one who only plays Mentor/Facilitator loses the contract. <strong>Behavioral complexity</strong> — enacting competing roles, often in the same week — predicts effectiveness. Now stress-test your portfolio against three live pressures: the CEO demanding the number, the two key engineers threatening to quit, and a hospital escalating a near-miss <em>adverse-event report</em>. Decide which control is non-negotiable.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Present and recover the 90-day plan`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `You deliver a four-minute plan to the executive committee — then the facilitator injects the recovery test: satisfaction has slipped from <strong>98% to 91%</strong> and throughput is still <strong>20% short</strong>. The trap is to whipsaw: reverse every change (you keep neither the old culture nor the new capability) or push control harder (you finish breaking the clan). <em>Recalibrating the balance is not the same as abandoning it.</em> Sequence a disciplined 90-day plan, pick the smallest effective adjustment, and commit to the four leading indicators you will actually watch.`,

                    r1_diagnosis_label:     `The OCAI profile of 90 staff is in. How do you read the unit's culture?`,
                    r1_gap_label:           `Which two quadrants must the unit ADD to meet the Scale-or-Stall mandate?`,
                    r1_naming_label:        `How candidly does your team name the contradiction — “we are being asked to become partly a Market culture”? (%)`,
                    r1_naming_readout:      `Willingness to name the tension instead of pretending it away:`,
                    diag_imbalanced:        `Imbalanced for the new mandate — strong Clan/Adhocracy, must ADD Market and Hierarchy`,
                    diag_broken:            `Broken — the relationship-driven culture is the problem and must be replaced`,
                    diag_fine:              `Fine as is — 98% satisfaction proves we should not change the culture`,
                    diag_market:            `Already a Market culture — the staff just need to be told the new numbers`,
                    gap_markethier:         `Market (results, SLAs, external customers) + Hierarchy (standardized, repeatable process)`,
                    gap_clanadhoc:          `More Clan + more Adhocracy — double down on relationships and craft`,
                    gap_hieronly:           `Hierarchy only — just standardize everything and the numbers follow`,
                    gap_marketonly:         `Market only — push results and let process sort itself out`,

                    r2_attn_label:          `Allocate the 100-point leadership-attention budget across the two CVF tensions (must total 100)`,
                    r2_attn_readout:        `Attention allocated:`,
                    r2_attn_cap:            `/ 100 points`,
                    attn_control:           `Toward Control & Market (process, SLAs, dashboards, results)`,
                    attn_flex:              `Toward Flexibility & Clan (relationships, craft, autonomy, trust)`,
                    r2_move1_label:         `First concrete move:`,
                    r2_move2_label:         `Second concrete move:`,
                    r2_move3_label:         `Third concrete move — protect what earns the 98%:`,
                    move_triage:            `Introduce a tiered triage process (Hierarchy — adds repeatable capacity)`,
                    move_callcenter:        `Convert the unit to a scripted call center (Hierarchy/Market — fast, breaks the clan)`,
                    move_hireonly:          `Just hire 120 people (the budget will not fund this)`,
                    move_dashboard:         `Publish a response-time dashboard (Market — makes results visible)`,
                    move_nodash:            `Keep negotiating deadlines case by case (Clan — no external SLA discipline)`,
                    move_secretmetrics:     `Track metrics privately and surprise people with them (Market, low trust)`,
                    move_craftlane:         `Protect a “craft-case” lane for complex patients (Clan — retains the engineers)`,
                    move_nolane:            `No protected lane — everything goes through the standard process`,
                    move_cutqa:             `Speed up by trimming the complaint-handling controls (drops 21 CFR 820)`,

                    r3_portfolio_label:     `Quinn's eight roles span four quadrants. Which role portfolio will your leadership team over-invest in this quarter?`,
                    r3_ceo_label:           `Pressure A — the CEO demands the throughput number now. Your response:`,
                    r3_engineers_label:     `Pressure B — the two key engineers (30% of relationships) threaten to quit. Your response:`,
                    r3_adverse_label:       `Pressure C — a hospital escalates a near-miss adverse-event report. Which control do you deliberately KEEP?`,
                    port_spanning:          `Spanning — Producer/Director (Market) AND Mentor/Facilitator (Clan): enact competing roles`,
                    port_clanonly:          `Comfortable — everyone plays Mentor and Facilitator (Clan only)`,
                    port_marketonly:        `Hard-charging — everyone plays Producer and Director (Market only)`,
                    port_hieronly:          `Process — everyone plays Monitor and Coordinator (Hierarchy only)`,
                    ceo_commit:             `Commit to a staged trajectory with leading indicators (Director + Monitor)`,
                    ceo_promise:            `Promise the full number on the original date, whatever it takes`,
                    ceo_deflect:            `Push back: the culture can't be rushed, ask for 18 more months`,
                    eng_enroll:             `Enroll them as craft-lane leaders and mentors of the new analysts (Mentor + Broker)`,
                    eng_ignore:             `Hold the line — anyone who won't scale can leave`,
                    eng_exempt:             `Exempt them from all change so they stay happy and isolated`,
                    adv_keepqa:             `Keep the 21 CFR 820 complaint-handling control non-negotiable, flex the rest (Monitor)`,
                    adv_speed:              `Downgrade the report to keep triage fast — speed is the mandate`,
                    adv_freezeall:          `Freeze the entire scale-up until every process is re-certified`,

                    r4_recovery_label:      `Mid-quarter signal: satisfaction slipped 98% → 91% AND throughput is still 20% short. Your recovery move:`,
                    r4_sequence_label:      `How do you sequence the 90-day plan you present to the executive committee?`,
                    r4_kpi_label:           `Which leading indicators do you commit to watch after the plan ships?`,
                    r4_steadiness_label:    `Steadiness of intent: how firmly do you hold the rebalanced course through turbulence rather than whipsawing? (%)`,
                    rec_recalibrate:        `Recalibrate — small adjustment to the balance, hold the transition steady`,
                    rec_reverse:            `Reverse everything — go back to the old craft culture to stop the slip`,
                    rec_harder:             `Push control harder — the slip means we haven't standardized enough`,
                    seq_phased:             `Phased — triage + craft lane first, dashboard next, full SLA at the first go-live`,
                    seq_announce:           `Announce “we are now a results culture” in an all-hands and move on`,
                    seq_bigbang:            `Big-bang — switch the whole unit to the new operating model on day one`,
                    kpi_balanced:           `All four — culture-fit, role balance, effectiveness AND stakeholder satisfaction`,
                    kpi_throughputonly:     `Throughput only — the number is what the board cares about`,
                    kpi_satonly:            `Satisfaction only — protect the score that made us special`,

                    warn_naming_range:      `Your candor on naming the contradiction must be a percentage between 0 and 100.`,
                    warn_attn_negative:     `Leadership-attention allocations cannot be negative.`,
