                    insight_bothand:        `Both/And leader: you scaled the clan without killing it — throughput on a credible trajectory to ≥70, the two key engineers retained, the 98% protected, and a leadership team enacting competing roles. You held the paradox instead of resolving it in one direction.`,
                    insight_overrotate:     `You hit the throughput number but broke the clan. The two engineers who held 30% of relationships are gone and satisfaction fell — you resolved the paradox toward Market/Hierarchy and lost the asset that made the number worth having.`,
                    insight_stayclan:       `You protected the beloved culture but missed the mandate. The throughput gap stayed open and the 24-hour SLA breached — resolving the paradox toward Clan forfeits the contract the board was counting on.`,
                    insight_stalled:        `You finished neither scaled nor protected — the worst of both. Re-examine the balance: a deliberate tilt toward control with a protected craft lane and spanning leadership roles beats every single-direction strategy.`,
                    insight_lostpeople:     `Over-rotation cost you the two senior engineers and the satisfaction score. Behavioral complexity — playing Mentor and Facilitator while you play Producer and Director — is what would have kept them through the scale-up.`,
                    insight_regulatory:     `You traded a 21 CFR 820 control for speed and triggered a regulatory event. Not all control is bureaucracy — adverse-event handling is non-negotiable. The both/and leader keeps that one and flexes elsewhere.`,
                    insight_whipsaw:        `You whipsawed on the recovery signal. Reversing the transition at the first dip left the unit with neither the old culture nor the new capability — recalibrating the balance, not abandoning it, is the disciplined recovery.`,
                    insight_lowrole:        `Role balance stayed low: your leadership team never spanned the competing quadrants. Mastery of one comfortable style predicts effectiveness far worse than the capacity to enact contradictory roles credibly.`,
                    insight_sla:            `SLA penalties accumulated — the unit breached the 24-hour clinical-response commitment it had never operated under. Visible response-time discipline (a Market/Hierarchy add) is what keeps those penalties off the board's report.`,

                    hint_overrotate:        `You're over-rotating to control — throughput climbs but the clan is breaking. Ease the balance back toward the engineers and protect the craft lane before the two key people walk.`,
                    hint_regulatory:        `You traded a non-negotiable 21 CFR 820 control for speed. Reinstate the complaint-handling control — a regulatory event costs far more than a slow case.`,
                    hint_role:              `Your leaders are stuck in one comfortable quadrant. Build a portfolio that spans Producer/Director and Mentor/Facilitator — behavioral complexity is what carries a both/and change.`,
                    hint_trust:             `Stakeholder trust is dangerously low — the engineers and the 98% are at risk. Protect the craft lane and enroll the key people as leaders of the transition.`,
                    hint_throughput:        `You're behind the throughput trajectory with little time left. Add repeatable capacity — tiered triage and a published dashboard — without industrializing the relationships.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong both/and position — throughput, trust and role balance all healthy. Now sequence the 90-day plan and commit to all four leading indicators so it survives the recovery test.`,

